DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions are used to retrieve and traverse DWARF Debugging Infor‐
     mation Entry (DIE) descriptors associated with a compilation unit.  These
     descriptors are arranged in the form of a tree, traversable using “child”
     and “sibling” links; see dwarf(3) for more information.  DWARF Debugging
     Information Entry descriptors are represented by the _D_w_a_r_f___D_i_e opaque
     type.

     Function ddwwaarrff__cchhiilldd() retrieves the child of descriptor denoted by argu‐
     ment _d_i_e, and stores it in the location pointed to by argument _r_e_t___d_i_e.

     Function ddwwaarrff__ssiibblliinnggooff() retrieves the sibling of the descriptor de‐
     noted by argument _d_i_e, and stores it in the location pointed to by argu‐
     ment _r_e_t___d_i_e.  If argument _d_i_e is NULL, the first debugging information
     entry descriptor for the current compilation unit will be returned.  This
     function and function ddwwaarrff__cchhiilldd() may be used together to traverse the
     tree of debugging information entry descriptors for a compilation unit.

     Function ddwwaarrff__ssiibblliinnggooff__bb() is identical to the function
     ddwwaarrff__ssiibblliinnggooff() except that it can retrieve the sibling descriptor from
     either the current compilation unit or type unit.  If argument _i_s___i_n_f_o is
     non-zero, the function behaves identically to function ddwwaarrff__ssiibblliinnggooff().
     If argument _i_s___i_n_f_o is zero, the descriptor referred by argument _d_i_e
     should be associated with a debugging information entry in the type unit.
     The function will store the sibling of the descriptor in the location
     pointed to by argument _r_e_t___d_i_e.  If argument _i_s___i_n_f_o is zero and argument
     _d_i_e is NULL, the first debugging information entry descriptor for the
     current type unit will be returned.

     Function ddwwaarrff__ooffffddiiee() retrieves the debugging information entry de‐
     scriptor at global offset _o_f_f_s_e_t in the “.debug_info” section of the ob‐
     ject associated with argument _d_b_g.  The returned descriptor is written to
     the location pointed to by argument _r_e_t___d_i_e.

     Function ddwwaarrff__ooffffddiiee__bb() is identical to the function ddwwaarrff__ooffffddiiee() ex‐
     cept that it can retrieve the debugging information entry descriptor at
     global offset _o_f_f_s_e_t from either of the “.debug_info” and “.debug_types”
     sections of the object associated with argument _d_b_g.  If argument _i_s___i_n_f_o
     is non-zero, the function will retrieve the debugging information entry
     from the “.debug_info” section, otherwise the function will retrieve the
     debugging information entry from the “.debug_types” section.  The re‐
     turned descriptor is written to the location pointed to by argument
     _r_e_t___d_i_e.

   MMeemmoorryy MMaannaaggeemmeenntt
     The memory area used for the _D_w_a_r_f___D_i_e descriptor returned in argument
     _r_e_t___d_i_e is allocated by the DWARF Access Library (libdwarf, -ldwarf).
     Application code should use function ddwwaarrff__ddeeaalllloocc() with the allocation
     type DW_DLA_DIE to free the memory area when the _D_w_a_r_f___D_i_e descriptor is
     no longer needed.

